At Sat, 26 Jan 2008 10:44:11 +0100,
Krzysztof Helt wrote:
> 
> From: Krzysztof Helt <krzysztof.h1@wp.pl>
> 
> This patch converts the Opti93x driver to use
> the cs4231 library instead of just duplicating the code.
> 
> Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Helt <krzysztof.h1@wp.pl>

This causes a compile error for snd-opti92x-cs4231.  Also has some
coding style issues.

The fixed patch is below.  Please let me know this and previous
patches work so that I can push them to the upstream.


Takashi

---

diff -r c62c921e2ffa isa/Kconfig
--- a/isa/Kconfig	Mon Jan 28 16:16:20 2008 +0100
+++ b/isa/Kconfig	Mon Jan 28 16:53:56 2008 +0100
@@ -321,7 +321,7 @@ config SND_OPTI93X
 	depends on SND
 	select SND_OPL3_LIB
 	select SND_MPU401_UART
-	select SND_PCM
+	select SND_CS4231_LIB
 	help
 	  Say Y here to include support for soundcards based on Opti
 	  82C93x chips.
diff -r c62c921e2ffa isa/opti9xx/opti92x-ad1848.c
--- a/isa/opti9xx/opti92x-ad1848.c	Mon Jan 28 16:16:20 2008 +0100
